{
  "//": [
    "deps[script]: the scripts it needs on every page that loads it; the page lists them, and before it when it reads their ns members at load time.",
    "late[script]: the scripts it only uses when they are there (a page may not load them, or a dep would close a cycle): read at run time behind a guard, never at load time.",
    "tools/module_graph.py (run by tools/build_page_css.py --check and the harness) fails when the code uses a script that its entry does not name, when an entry names an unused script, on a deps cycle, and when a page lists a script without one of its deps.",
    "The script modules of every page shell, in load order: the one list app_loader.js, app.js, the page controllers and tools/build_page_css.py read.",
    "common: loaded first on every page (shared helpers and UI components: add a new app_ui_<name>.js here, after app_dom.js; app_router.js, ns.router, owns the address bar).",
    "pages.<page>.bootstrap: the page controller the shell starts; modules: loaded at start, after common;",
    "lazy.<group>: loaded on first use through ns.loader.loadGroup(group).",
    "A module's stylesheet rules ship on a page only when the module is listed for it. Edit this file, then run python3 tools/build_page_css.py:",
    "it copies each page's entry into its shell (<script id=\"chdashModules\">) and rebuilds the page stylesheets.",
    "pages.explorer, pages.functions (explorer.html, functions.html, app.js): the Explorer's Catalog (/explorer[/<db>[/<table>]]) and its Functions (/explorer/_functions[/<name>]) are two pages of their own; the Functions page loads the Explorer module and the highlighter, none of the graph, treemap, storage or table card modules.",
    "pages.system, pages.queries, pages.disks (system.html, queries.html, disks.html, app_system.js): each System section is a page of its own, at /system, /system/queries and /system/disks: app_system_view.js (the shared pieces and the section's filter bar) and the section's module (the Overview: app_system_activity.js, app_system_perf.js and app_system_overview.js after the treemap for its databases; Queries: app_system_queries.js with app_meta.js for the highlighter; Disks: app_system_disks.js after the treemap), after the chart engine, the filter bar and the time range picker.",
    "pages.traces, pages.logs, pages.metrics (traces.html, logs.html, metrics.html, app_obs_page.js): each Observability view is a page of its own, at /observability/<view>: the modules every view needs, then the view's own (the Traces ones, the Logs ones, the Metrics ones).",
    "pages.trace (trace.html, app_trace_page.js): one trace at /observability/traces/<trace id>, a page of its own: the trace view modules of the Traces view without the search ones.",
    "pages.shape (shape.html, app_shape_page.js): one query shape at /system/queries/<hash>, a page of its own: the System view and its Queries section, none of the other sections; app_meta.js gives the highlighter the host's function and keyword lists, as on the Query page.",
    "pages.mcp (mcp.html, app_mcp_page.js): the MCP integration page at /mcp-integration, a page of its own and not tied to a host: the access keys of the MCP endpoint. app_mcp_view.js draws the header block and the keys table, app_mcp_form.js the key form and the secret panel (after the dialog), and every request goes through the ns.api functions of app_api.js.",
    "app_ui_filterbar.js (ns.filterBar): the filter bar of Observability and System, and the bar of the MCP page (status, Refresh, New key); listed on those pages only (its rules ship where it can be built)."
  ],
